WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.050
The new Freedom Ranking is out.

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.320
Every year, researchers

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.560
at the Fraser and Cato Institutes

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.090
compare economic freedoms

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:07.644
like the

00:00:07.644 --> 00:00:08.980
freedom to trade,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.560
amount of regulations,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.560
tax levels,

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.060
plus

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.400
personal freedoms like

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.520
women’s rights

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.450
and religious freedom.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.720
They publish the results

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.939
in the Human Freedom Index.

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:22.760
It compares countries according to how free they are.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.279
So, is America

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.340
the freest country?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.520
No.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.300
We came in 17th this year,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.660
well behind many other countries.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.820
The report says

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.780
the freest countries are now:

00:00:34.787 --> 00:00:35.520
Switzerland

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.440
Hong Kong

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.610
New Zealand

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.400
Ireland

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.830
and then Australia.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:40.330
Years ago,

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.213
America was near the top of the

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.460
economic freedom list.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.480
The United States used to have

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.480
one of the freest economies in the world.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.880
Ian Vasquez helped write the rankings.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.968
It used to be 2, 3, or 4

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.160
and then

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.860
government started to grow.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.280
It started to spend more.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.760
To step in with dramatic government action

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.280
and regulate more.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.760
The strongest

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.620
consumer financial protections

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.600
in history

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.040
and tax more.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.080
Those who are more fortunate

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.360
are going to have to pay a little bit more.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.200
Those are reasons

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.200
we fell on the freedom list.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.420
So let’s look at the top of the list.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.320
Why does

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.389
Switzerland rank

00:01:15.389 --> 00:01:16.800
first in the world?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.740
Welcome to the world.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.480
Because it has comparatively little regulation,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.700
low taxes,

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.800
a free press,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.960
and other freedoms

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:26.480
like same-sex marriage

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.900
that many other countries lack.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.040
A good ranking matters,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.420
not just because it’s good to be free,

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.660
but because freedom

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.860
allows people to prosper.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.400
Look what happened in Hong Kong,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.080
number 2 on the list.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.560
Hong Kong,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.020
a thousand worlds in this one small spot.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.100
Not long ago,

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.160
people in Hong Kong

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.019
were among the poorest in the world,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:48.680
but now

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.020
they're among the richest.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.120
What do I like about Hong Kong?

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.300
Every moment there’s something exciting going on.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.400
Prosperity happened

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.120
because Hong Kong’s government

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.139
put few obstacles in the way of

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:02.599
trying new things,

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:04.539
like starting a business.

00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:05.100
Here I am

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:05.780
in Hong Kong,

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.420
years ago,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.480
applying for legal permission to open a business.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.200
Handing in one form

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.680
was all I had to do.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.860
Thank you, sir.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.470
The next morning I opened Stossel Enterprises.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.470
Ten dollars.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.077
It was a stupid business

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.200
selling things like

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.740
American frisbees,

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.120
but that chance to try new things

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.470
is what allowed Hong Kong to prosper.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.100
By comparison, India ranks much lower

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.701
because there,

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:34.160
to start a business, entrepreneurs

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.600
may have to wait years

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.680
while bureaucrats like these

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.080
debate the merit of your idea.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.760
Good ideas die,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.460
waiting

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.680
on these shelves.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.640
That’s a reason

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.240
India stays poor.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.520
It could be worse.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.094
The most oppressed people in the world

00:02:50.094 --> 00:02:52.110
are those who live in the countries at the bottom

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.500
of the freedom ranking:

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.320
Egypt

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.040
Yemen

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:55.780
Libya

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.880
Venezuela

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.060
and least free,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.020
Syria.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.560
Mostly because of the war.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.320
You aren’t free

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.140
if you worry about being killed.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.740
“No alimento”

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.800
2nd least free country Venezuela

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.660
was once

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.080
the richest country in Latin America.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.900
Then Socialists promised

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.400
they'd spread the wealth.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.000
Now Venezuelans fight over bags of flour.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.637
Freedom is under attack

00:03:22.637 --> 00:03:24.060
all around the word.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.740
Tanja Porcnik is the rankings other author.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.080
I interviewed her by Skype,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:28.900
because

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.132
she now lives in Austria,

00:03:30.132 --> 00:03:31.500
although she was born in

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.580
Slovakia.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.560
You moved to Austria to get more freedom?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.640
Ah, yes.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.400
Freedom just inspired me.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.860
Freedom

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.060
relates to other things that matter.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.860
What’s important in life?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.520
Those of us who revere freedom

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.980
often say it’s the

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.960
dignity of the individual,

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.400
and a chance to live

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.840
free from coercion.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.120
You can lead your life

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.200
any way you want

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.180
as long as you respect the equal rights of others.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.020
What job you want to take,

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.140
what kinds of things you want to do,

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.980
who you want to marry,

00:04:00.981 --> 00:04:02.307
what you want to do on your free time,

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:03.110
where you want to live.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.230
Countries don’t regulate your free time.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.606
Oh yes they do,

00:04:06.606 --> 00:04:08.900
they regulate everything.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.160
They regulate vacation time,

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.360
where you can travel,

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.380
if you’re a woman in some part of the world,

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.940
you have to ask permission from men

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.000
to go out in public.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.740
Freedom brings good things

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.280
to countries that try it.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:22.780
People now

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.240
want to live in 3rd-ranked New Zealand.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.784
The country is politically and economically stable

00:04:27.784 --> 00:04:29.820
with people all over the world attracted

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.480
by the benefits and opportunities.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.260
Ireland

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.620
used to be poor,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.220
but now it ranks 4th on the Freedom Index.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.355
You don't just arrive in Ireland,

00:04:41.355 --> 00:04:42.000
you jump in.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.420
Ireland, I think about the potato famine.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.540
I don’t think about prosperity.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.850
They reduced taxes.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.510
They reduced spending.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.540
They reduced some regulations.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.280
They opened up to trade.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.910
Crack down on China’s trade abuses.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:00.100
America now may close itself to some trade.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.100
If that makes you want to move

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.240
to another country,

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.920
the rankings offer places to consider.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.460
And places to avoid…

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.780
Greece is beautiful,

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.480
but it ranks 60th in freedom.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.480
China has gotten richer,

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.960
but it ranks 130th.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.659
You can read the full rankings

00:05:20.659 --> 00:05:21.985
on the Cato Institute’s

00:05:21.985 --> 00:05:23.960
and Fraser Institute’s websites.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.100
It’s too bad

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.180
that the US is now only 17th in the rankings,

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.380
but the good news is that

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:30.240
we are 17th

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.401
partly because

00:05:31.401 --> 00:05:32.520
in recent years,

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.260
other countries became more free.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.404
Despite what we hear on the news,

00:05:37.404 --> 00:05:38.787
over several decades,

00:05:38.787 --> 00:05:40.145
the world has slowly

00:05:40.145 --> 00:05:40.960
been getting

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:41.720
better.

